{
 "about": "The judgments chapter 35 adds to the dataset records: each corpus's data type, the stretch of the spine it shows, the persons and images figures read from its record, and whether it has been tried. Written by hand on 2026-10-24 from data/sources/<id>.json (its what, level_truth and status lines) and data/registry/<id>.json (its regions); tools/data_figures.py reads it with the records and writes corpora.json. A span marked stated is the record's own words; inferred is read from the body part the collection images (chest, abdomen, pelvis, whole body). tried is yes where the record's status says a bank, a run or a test of the reported stack used it.",
 "types": {
  "paired": "paired 3D-2D: real 2D frames or projections with a CT or CBCT of the same body",
  "annotated": "annotated 2D: real radiographs, fluoroscopy or cine with spine labels (boxes, landmarks, levels or grades)",
  "synthetic": "synthetic 2D: renders or generated images (and synthetic CTs) with exact or inherited labels",
  "ct": "CT volumes: 3D collections, the raw material of synthetic 2D and of the CT counting priors",
  "unannotated": "unannotated 2D: real images with no spine labels, for unsupervised or self-supervised use"
 },
